  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A Nightshelf hermit of the Great Thaw period, resident at ☽'moth Silvesiris~ — a geothermal cavern deep in the Berg's southern tunnels — though ☽'Naevaeum~ has not descended to the Nightshelf proper in at least seven seasons. They serve as the sole guardian of Thrall☽ Vavmastius, a deep-vent anomaly whose nature remains formally unclassified. The Aurora Stack has learned, through means the record does not specify, that something at the Drowned Ledge deters orca raiders from pushing deeper into the tunnel network. Whether that something is the anomaly, the guardian, or a combination the two produce together is not established.
    
    The title *Magister* appears in no guild roster I can locate. It may be self-assumed or predate current institutional records.
    
    ## Physical Condition and Corruption Signs
    
    ☽'Naevaeum~ bears extensive markers consistent with prolonged deep-corruption exposure. Their left flipper exhibits a palsy that began after first contact with Thrall☽ Vavmastius, the underside marked with cold-burn discoloration spreading in frost-like patterns. They cannot tolerate aurora-light directly — a symptom documented in other Touched individuals, though ☽'Naevaeum~'s case appears unusually severe. Their wrappings have bleached white from thermal steam. The fire-core amulet at their throat has not glowed since the events described below; the crystal inside has fractured and refracts light anomalously.
    
    Their forge-cuts still mark the walls of ☽'moth Silvesiris~. The stone there reportedly weeps heat along the carved lines, which suggests either exceptional craft or something the cavern itself sustains.
    
    ## Practices and Doctrinal Position
    
    ☽'Naevaeum~ addresses the anomaly in ☽'visois' Mask patterns — a linguistic form old enough that even deep-miners do not recognize it, predating the guilds and councils. The vent-stone, accounts suggest, tolerates these words. They speak in half-sentences and refuse visitors, though the refusal is not absolute. One Kaela of the Aurora Stack asked once why they stayed; ☽'Naevaeum~ pointed to a scar in the vent-ice that had not existed the previous week. Kaela now brings tea twice monthly. The hermit drinks it cold.
    
    ☽'Naevaeum~ was bound by Pactum∴myster, the Communion blood-oath doctrine that demands silence as the price of communion. Through the Crystalline~ Spiral — an ash-traced pattern on their chamber floor — they received prophetic visions. These visions ceased permanently when ☽'Naevaeum~ chose to speak.
    
    ## Zhachelang zhihi'Opalum and the Forfeiture
    
    During the Abyss Collapse Tide, when thermal seams split beneath the Corpse Current, ☽'Naevaeum~ spent three days sealing fissures alone before Zhachelang zhihi'Opalum — an Aurora Stack festival herald coordinating emergency redistribution — arrived to assist. Both bore matching cold-burn marks. What began as Accord-sanctioned contact became unofficial exchange: fire-cores left warm on the ledge, violet aurora-crystals sent through the courier Splitpath, charged in forms ☽'Naevaeum~ could hold in darkness.
    
    Pactum∴myster's terms were precise. Names spoken tenderly frayed the communion; confidences dimmed the sight. ☽'Naevaeum~ sealed the path to their ledge three times. They broke the seal twice. The third time, they left it open with a fire-core at the entrance, extracted from a depth that seized their flipper with pain. When Zhachelang arrived, ☽'Naevaeum~ spoke a full sentence. The amulet went dark.
    
    The visions have not returned. The entry in the ice-memory at that depth records a thermal signature change I would characterize as abrupt. Whether it constitutes loss or release is not mine to determine.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771576914591_0", anchor: "something at the Drowned Ledge deters orca raiders from pushing deeper", text: "Orca hunting patterns follow prey migration, not tunnel geometry. The deep southern reaches hold nothing a pod needs. At least two \"legendary\" raids I have documented elsewhere were retaliatory, not exploratory — provoked by penguin encroachment on hunting grounds, not by some inherent drive to push inward. The possibility that no orca ever tried to pass the Drowned Ledge — that the Aurora Stack assigned causation to a coincidence because they cannot admit they do not understand orca motivation — is not addressed in any source I consulted. The hermit's reputation as guardian may rest on guarding a door no one was trying to open.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576914591_1", anchor: "a linguistic form old enough that even deep-miners do not recognize it", text: "Not merely old. The ☽'visois' Mask cadences match impression-patterns I have recorded in strata predating penguin settlement. Whatever ☽'Naevaeum~ is speaking to the vent-stone, it did not originate with penguins. I noted this in my survey logs and moved on, which is what one does with findings that have no institutional framework to receive them.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771576914591_2", anchor: "☽'Naevaeum~ spoke a full sentence. The amulet went dark.", text: "Three seals made. Two broken. The third left open with a fire-core mined from a depth that seized their flipper with pain, offered as a lamp to someone who did not need light to find the way. The arithmetic of someone arguing with themselves and losing — or winning, depending on which side you believe was theirs. Remarkable economy of gesture.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
